WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.510
This video shows how to run several basins
in one go and read the table of the run.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.532
This video runs five basins together:

00:00:09.532 --> 00:00:16.100
the basin 02070002, North Branch Potomac,
and four small HUC8 models.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.541
In Set-up, click Clear choice.

00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:20.791
Tick each model that you want to run.

00:00:20.991 --> 00:00:23.616
The line beside the heading of the list
says how

00:00:23.616 --> 00:00:26.131
many models are found and how many are
chosen.

00:00:33.224 --> 00:00:34.604
Click Continue to Run.

00:00:37.797 --> 00:00:41.339
With several models chosen, the Run page
runs them together,

00:00:41.339 --> 00:00:45.707
and the line beside its heading says how
many basins are chosen in Set-up.

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:50.693
Each basin runs with the years, warm-up
and tables set for it in Set-up.

00:00:51.193 --> 00:00:55.473
The table lists each basin with its years,
its warm-up and the word ready.

00:00:55.979 --> 00:01:00.059
Checks before the run has one line for
each thing that SWATrust checked.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.460
The block Threads has two boxes.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.320
Basins at once sets how many basins run at
the same time.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.118
Threads in each basin sets the number of

00:01:09.118 --> 00:01:12.170
threads that the engine uses inside each
basin.

00:01:12.679 --> 00:01:15.039
The number of threads is a setting of the
run.

00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:16.979
It changes no input file.

00:01:17.179 --> 00:01:18.999
Both boxes may stay empty.

00:01:19.499 --> 00:01:20.679
Click Start the run.

00:01:22.487 --> 00:01:25.407
The button Stop all now stands where the
start button stood.

00:01:25.607 --> 00:01:28.567
Watch the lines under Basin, progress and
threads.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:33.457
Each basin has a line with its state:
Running, and then Finished, with its years.

00:01:33.981 --> 00:01:37.451
The runs take a while, and the video goes
on when they have ended.

00:01:40.657 --> 00:01:42.495
When every basin has finished,

00:01:42.495 --> 00:01:46.477
the page shows the table of the run, with
one row for each basin.

00:01:46.984 --> 00:01:48.424
Click the row of a basin.

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:51.700
Run details under the table then shows
that basin:

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.714
its number of threads, its years and its
warm-up.

00:01:55.216 --> 00:01:58.446
SWATrust writes the table of the run to
the

00:01:58.446 --> 00:02:01.526
file basins.csv in the folder of the run.

00:02:01.726 --> 00:02:05.166
Above the table stands the button Save the
table (CSV).

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:09.427
Click Results in a row to open that basin
in the Results view.

00:02:09.627 --> 00:02:12.537
There, the box Basin chooses the basin to
show.

00:02:13.039 --> 00:02:17.359
The next chapter, Calibrate and validate,
fits a basin to measured flow.
